    "description": "Divide payment according to work contribution and recover daily earnings.",
    "teachingApproach": "Tie wages directly to work share. Start with two workers who work for the same duration, then add a helper, different working durations, daily wage ratios, and reverse earning questions. Keep job-payment shares separate from time spent: rate × time determines contribution, and contribution determines payment.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 30,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 17, Time and Work. Approved scope: Teach that payment for a completed job is divided in the ratio of work contributions, not simply time spent. Cover two-worker wage splits from completion times, a helper added to finish early, daily wage ratios combined with different days worked, recovering daily wages from total earnings, a fixed fund paying workers for different numbers of days, and efficiency-linked wage comparisons. Include the chapter pattern of A+B and B+C work fractions to recover A's share."
  },
